    "Square entries document more administrative and governance dysfunction — unresponsiveness, favoritism/athletic/wealth bias, leadership turnover, fiscal scandal and punitive or opaque policies — than circle entries": "This bucket captures systemic governance and policy failures (favoritism, pay‑to‑play, opaque/authoritarian discipline, fiscal mismanagement and leadership problems) which are about institutional decision‑making and priorities and therefore separate from the other buckets that focus on student safety incidents or uneven classroom/IEP/counseling experiences.",
    "square entries report more failures and strain in student support services, counseling, and special education compliance than circle entries": "This bucket isolates pervasive capacity and compliance problems in support services (understaffed/unresponsive counseling departments, IEP/504 noncompliance, punitive handling of struggling students and overloaded counselors) and is kept distinct from the 'within‑school variability' bucket by emphasizing systemic service strain and noncompliance across the school rather than polarizing 'pockets' of excellent versus poor support."
}"]

